    {
      "code": "OPERATIONS_MANAGER",
      "cross_product": false,
      "description": "Raises, approves and receives purchase orders org-wide; maintains suppliers and inventory (including stock adjustments); reads warehouses. Accepts, cancels and hands over customer orders \u2014 the stock-commitment, stock-release and billing-gate steps \u2014 on top of the ordinary counter work every Operations user does, and hands orders to a carrier (the same billing gate, on the delivery path). Opens, reviews and closes cycle counts and approves the discrepancies they raise (ADR-0026). Registers lots and rolls, splits and merges rolls, moves stock between bins and statuses, and reads stock and the ledger (ADR-0014 Phase 1). Takes and refunds orders' online payments and reads the payment reconciliation. Does not create or rename warehouses, or connect or change the organization's payment-provider account \u2014 those stay with the admin. Creates floors and edits a draft layout's placements and walk graph, but does not publish one \u2014 a floor plan going live is as dangerous as it gets here, so that stays with the admin too.",
